### `time_passed` (REQUIRED FIELD, 1x ONLY)

Use this to report how much elapsed in-world wall-clock time the concrete non-travel actions in the text realistically consumed. Estimate elapsed wall-clock time, not reading time and not the sum of each participant's labor when characters work in parallel. 

```xml
<timePassed>
  <reasoning>Brief breakdown of time-consuming actions</reasoning>
  <duration>Exact duration rounded to the nearest minute, 1 minute minimum (typical for conversation and quick scenes). No time ranges, unknowns, or other nonspecific answers. Format with one of: "HH:MM", "[INTEGER] [minutes/hours]", or "[INTEGER] hours, [INTEGER] minutes".</duration>
</timePassed>
#}
### `in_combat`{% if not tinyBrainEventSchema %} (REQUIRED FIELD, 1x ONLY){% endif %}

Use this to indicate whether the player should currently be considered in physical combat, even if the player did not personally attack during the text.

```xml
<inCombat>
  <value>true|false</value>
</inCombat>
```

### `anyQuestObjectivesCompleted`{% if not tinyBrainEventSchema %} (REQUIRED FIELD, 1x ONLY){% endif %}

Use this to indicate if it's likely that any quest objectives were completed. This will trigger a full quest objective check, so it doesn't require any additional comment.

```xml
<anyQuestObjectivesCompleted>
  <value>true|false</value>
</anyQuestObjectivesCompleted>
```

### `tracker_updates` (OPTIONAL FIELD, 0-1x)

Use this to report any changes to the values of existing trackers, or to add new trackers for things that should be tracked but don't have them yet. Include only trackers that changed or that should be added or removed; omit unchanged trackers.

<trackerUpdates>
  <trackerUpdate>
    <trackerName>Exact tracker name</trackerName>
    <type>countdown|numerical_count|x_out_of_total|percentage|short_string</type>
    <action>update|add|remove</action>
    <newValue>New tracker value, if add or update; use "none" for remove. Strictly format depending on type: 'countdown' → concrete duration until the deadline, such as "HH:MM", "[INTEGER] [days/minutes/hours]", or "[INTEGER] days, [INTEGER] hours, [INTEGER] minutes" (the game stores an absolute deadline and displays remaining time automatically); 'numerical_count' → integer; 'x_out_of_total' → "[NUMBER]/[NUMBER]"; 'percentage' → integer between 0 and 100, with or without a percent sign; 'short_string' → string no more than {{ shortStringTrackerMaxWords | default(4) }} words. No approximate values (2-3 days, about 10 minutes, etc) allowed; no units except as specified</newValue>
    <reason>One sentence reason for the update</reason>
  </trackerUpdate>
  <!-- Repeat trackerUpdate for each updated, added, or removed tracker. If no trackers are updated, omit the trackerUpdates block or leave it empty. -->
</trackerUpdates>

## End XML schema

As a rule, the events are meant to ensure that the tracked game starts matches the prose, so  for insurance, before assuming an item is already tracked, check whether it appears in itemsInScene or any character's inventory. Items referenced in prose or offscreen updates that don't appear in these lists should be recorded when they first become physically present. Give similar consideration to NPCs and other entities that are not already known to be present. If the text describes something that should be tracked but is not already tracked, include an event for its first appearance.
